# The mirror of combat-first-strike-prevents-return-damage: there the
# ATTACKER had first strike; here the BLOCKER does. Silvercoat Lion (2/2, no
# keywords) attacks; Elvish Archers (2/1, First Strike) blocks. dealsInStep
# (combatdamage.go) is keyed off each creature's own keyword regardless of
# attacker/blocker role, so the Archers' 2 power is exactly lethal to the
# Lion's 2 toughness in the first-strike step -- the advance into Combat
# Damage runs the state-based-action check that kills the Lion before the
# regular step ever asks whether it deals damage back.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 2=1
declareblockers
advance
firststrikedamage
advance
combatdamage
